{"id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#cor:r2-not-homeomorphic-rn","title":"cor:r2-not-homeomorphic-rn","path":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.md","line":247,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex#cor:r2-not-homeomorphic-rn","uses":["[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#prop:pi1-of-product-space]]","[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#prop:pi1-sphere-trivial-n-geq-2]]","[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#thm:fundamental-group-of-circle]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex","label":"cor:r2-not-homeomorphic-rn","line":407,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[$\\R^2$ is not homeomorphic to $\\R^n$ for $n \\ne 2$]\n\\label{cor:r2-not-homeomorphic-rn}\n\n\\uses{prop:pi1-of-product-space, prop:pi1-sphere-trivial-n-geq-2, thm:fundamental-group-of-circle}\n\n\\dcref{ch1:1.16}\n\\group{Fundamental Group}\n\n$\\R^2$ is not homeomorphic to $\\R^n$ for $n\\ne2$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch For $n=1$, deleting a point leaves $\\R^2$ connected but $\\R$ disconnected.\nFor $n>2$, $\\R^n-\\{x\\}\\simeq S^{n-1}$ has trivial fundamental group,\nwhereas $\\R^2-\\{0\\}\\simeq S^1$ has fundamental group $\\Z$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[<span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\R ^2$\">$\\R ^2$</span> is not homeomorphic to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\R ^n$\">$\\R ^n$</span> for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n \\ne 2$\">$n \\ne 2$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a72322d6e6f742d686f6d656f6d6f72706869632d726e\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FHatcher%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fcha